  "salt": "r9eGVoomBM4tE1xWUw3bYA==",
  "text": "Diarmait UA DUIBNE descended from the obscure goddess DUBINN. He was the most famous mythological hero of this name. Diarmait was the fated lover of GRÁINNE. Gráinne was young and beautiful. She was betrothed to the aging FIONN MAC CUMHAILL. A magical woman gave Diarmait a love spot. The source names this mark the ball seirc. The spot sat on his forehead. It made him irresistible to women. Some tales hid the spot under bangs. A breeze lifted his hair at a feast in Fionn's hall. Gráinne spied the spot and fell in love. A GEIS forbade Diarmait from refusing a woman who came neither mounted nor on foot. She came at sundown riding a mule. This fulfilled the geis. Diarmait and Gráinne fled through Ireland. Fionn and the FIANNA pursued them. The stones where they slept were prehistoric DOLMENS. People call them beds of Diarmait and Gráinne. Legend counts 366 dolmens in Ireland. That number matches a leap year spent fleeing. Fionn caught the pair in the forest of Dubros in Co. Sligo. Diarmait hid in a HAZEL tree. A wild BOAR killed Diarmait on Ben Bulben. Only Fionn could heal that bleeding.",
  "objective": "Diarmait UA DUIBNE was a mythological Irish hero. He was the fated lover of GRÁINNE.",
